  <p>Nauru's history spans over three millennia, from the first Micronesian navigators who crossed the Pacific in outrigger canoes, through the upheavals of colonialism and world wars, to its emergence as the world's smallest independent republic. Few nations of any size have a story as dramatic — boom and bust, survival against the odds, and a people whose identity has endured through every challenge.</p>

